  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner-decision 2026-08-27">This class is fixed HERE, not offloaded. The owner's words: "trying to offload to other projects is very risky because they lack the context." Filing a finding for another project to fix is NOT an acceptable outcome for any row.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The authorization key and the container MUST be the same value, derived from `(entity, recordId)`. A route accepting BOTH a record and a container is a failed implementation — that is option (B), which was rejected.</constraint>
    <constraint source="§11 reuse">Reuse `RecordContainerResolver`, `CallerRecordAccessProbe`, `EntityAccessFilter`, and `TryResolveParentEntitySet`. A second resolver, probe, or entity-set map is a review failure.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">A secure record with no container FAILS CLOSED and loudly. Never a fallback.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Authorization is an endpoint filter, not handler code and not middleware.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">DELETE rather than convert where a path is dead. Verify deadness first-hand — 076 found the chunked pair's client depended on a route mapped nowhere.</constraint>
    <constraint source="sequencing">Do NOT edit the three Compose files while PR #806 is open. Verify with `gh api --paginate`, never `gh pr view --json files`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task-074">Delete waivers for routes that become gated or deleted. Do NOT convert a Pending waiver to Permanent to make a build green — that inverts the forcing function.</constraint>
    <constraint source="tests/CLAUDE.md">Any new ArchTest rule carries BOTH a negative and a positive control.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Placement Justification citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; publish size ≤60 MB (baseline 44.96 incl. PDBs — state the five-field convention); CVE check.</constraint>
  </constraints>

